// REQUESTS 19: a tuplet drawn WITHOUT its number (and its bracket), for the OMR's training pages.
// An engraver prints the "3" over the first triplets only, or none where the music plainly runs
// in threes: Beethoven's Op.27/2 (Moonlight) prints it in bar 1 only (Scoring Notes 2024's
// Sibelius PDF), Schumann's Op.15/1 nowhere. Triplets with no number are the largest cause of the
// OMR's errors on its evaluation set (942 notes, 24 %), and the generator cannot draw them: lysc
// 0.14.0 has no layout key for it and refuses 'override TupletNumber.transparent = true' and
// 'override TupletBracket.transparent = true' (LYS1029).
// Bars 1-2: triplets as lysc draws them now (beamed eighths: the number; quarters: number and bracket).
// Bars 3-4: the same music, to be drawn with no number and no bracket (the spelling is Lily#'s to choose;
// LilyPond 2.26.0: \omit TupletNumber \omit TupletBracket, see the .ly beside this).
octave absolute
title "Tuplets without numbers"
time 4/4
key c major
part rh {
  clef treble
  section A {
    tuplet 3/2 { g'8 c'' e'' } tuplet 3/2 { g'8 c'' e'' } tuplet 3/2 { g'8 c'' e'' } tuplet 3/2 { g'8 c'' e'' } |
    tuplet 3/2 { c''4 d'' e'' } tuplet 3/2 { f''4 e'' d'' } |
    tuplet 3/2 { a'8 c'' e'' } tuplet 3/2 { a'8 c'' e'' } tuplet 3/2 { a'8 c'' e'' } tuplet 3/2 { a'8 c'' e'' } |
    tuplet 3/2 { c''4 d'' e'' } tuplet 3/2 { f''4 e'' d'' } |
  }
}
form { A }
score { staff rh }
